comments[17]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-31T14:40:25.095Z","harness:codex","Scope selected after all-status and GitHub intake: co-deliver pm-xm0id4 and pm-2ew0w3 because both expose CLI-private lifecycle policy that must become SDK-owned. No other item is in progress."
  "2026-07-31T15:21:34.990Z","harness:codex","Delivery evidence: close transaction ownership moved under src/sdk/lifecycle; lifecycle policy is public, individually testable, selectable by SDK consumers, and shared by CLI/MCP. The CLI close module is now a compatibility shim; public surface snapshot records 24 classified additive exports. Fresh npm and Bun consumers installed the packed 2026.7.31 tarball, imported closeItem and policy primitives from @unbrained/pm-cli/sdk, and ran contained npx/bunx binaries. Full coverage passed 6,610 tests at 100/100/100/100. Remaining create/update/delete/restore/context SDK-to-CLI inversions mean the broad item is intentionally not complete in this PR."
  "2026-07-31T15:49:45.896Z","harness:codex",The generated error-code catalog was refreshed after moving close implementation ownership; close-family error source provenance now names sdk/lifecycle/close.ts rather than the CLI shim.
  "2026-07-31T16:10:53.522Z","harness:codex","Review loop evidence: regenerated the full runtime contract snapshot; canonicalized close target ids; shared one tracker scan across active-child and auto-unblock analysis; and verified 6,613 tests at 100/100/100/100 plus static quality. CI root cause was only a stale generated contract fixture."
  "2026-07-31T20:18:34.790Z","harness:codex","Scope 2026-07-31: finish the remaining SDK-to-CLI lifecycle inversion with a hard import-boundary gate and SDK-owned operation contracts; co-deliver cross-surface provenance and published-artifact acceptance so CLI, MCP, npm, npx, and bunx exercise the same public substrate."
  "2026-07-31T21:34:34.527Z","harness:codex","Delivery evidence 2026-07-31: SDK ownership now covers close, get, copy, delete, restore, and focus; the former CLI modules are thin compatibility exports, runtime and index expose direct SDK primitives, and the public-surface/error/contract snapshots are regenerated. The full suite passed 6,623 tests at exact 100/100/100/100, with static SDK-boundary, package-parity, docstring, and context-budget gates green. Fresh packed-package npm and Bun smoke/agent sessions also pass. This item remains active because create, update, context, next, and plan still require the same ownership inversion before its complete lifecycle acceptance criterion can close."
  "2026-07-31T22:25:40.124Z","harness:codex","Review-loop evidence 2026-07-31: CodeRabbit identified that SDK get materialized optional children/tree keys as undefined. The SDK-owned query now omits absent projections, preserving serialized contract semantics; regression tests cover both flat and tree reads. The complete 409-file suite passes 6,625 tests at exact 100/100/100/100, and quality:static passes its SDK boundary, package parity, token-budget, surface, import-cost, transport, and 100% docstring gates. Remaining create/update/context/next/plan inversion stays explicitly open."
  "2026-08-01T05:27:11.225Z","harness:codex","Delivery evidence 2026-08-01: removed every src/sdk -> src/cli import and made create/update/plan/append/claim/bulk lifecycle, context/activity/aggregate/calendar/history/next, annotations, guide/completion, reindex/upgrade, runtime contracts, and registration helpers SDK-owned. CLI command modules are thin compatibility exports or removed orphan shims. The static gate now parses TypeScript import/export/require forms and hard-fails any SDK-to-CLI edge. Public aggregate, query, and governance entrypoints expose the owned operations; the regenerated surface records additive contracts. Exact full coverage passes 6,652 tests at 100/100/100/100; quality:static, ESLint, contracts, surface, package parity, token calibration, import cost, and transport gates pass. Isolated packed npm and Bun consumers resolved contained binaries and 20 operation exports; npx and bunx plus a temporary init/create/claim/update/context/list/close lifecycle passed."
  "2026-08-01T05:29:04.464Z","harness:codex","Changelog evidence: npm registry latest pm-changelog is 2026.7.29-1; the project installed that exact version, regenerated CHANGELOG.md from closed PM items, and changelog:pm:check returned unchanged for 1,872 items."
  "2026-08-01T05:40:27.418Z","harness:codex","PR evidence 2026-08-01: broad SDK substrate, context calibration, provenance parity, and package conformance delivery published as GitHub PR #850 https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/850 at implementation commit a5be2cda39c1072906265bb6120325600cc38523. Exact-head release gates and AI review loop are pending."
  "2026-08-01T05:56:35.837Z","harness:codex","Exact-head CI feedback 2026-08-01: PR #850 exposed a cross-platform acceptance timeout and four DeepScan relocation findings. The real calibration entrypoint exceeded its 120-second test ceiling on Windows, so the test now allows 300 seconds; two unused imports and two unused local parameters were removed from SDK-owned modules. Focused 118 tests, quality:static, context calibration, contracts, SDK surface/import-cost, package parity, and transport gates pass."
  "2026-08-01T06:03:23.713Z","harness:codex","CI lint follow-up 2026-08-01: after accepting DeepScan's dead-code findings, strict ESLint correctly rejected stale suppression entries. Pruned the obsolete registration-helper suppressions and normalized the suppression manifest. Full pnpm lint now passes ESLint, zero jscpd clones, static quality, 100% docstrings, SDK/package boundaries, intent calibration, gate registry, SDK surface/import costs, and transport floors."
  "2026-08-01T06:12:07.880Z","harness:codex","CI follow-up evidence (PR #850): decoded coverage shard 4's Vitest blob report and identified the sole failure as the release automation contract retaining the pre-prune ESLint suppression baseline. Burned the mandatory suppression budget down from 129 to the actual 127 in package.json, the static gate default, and its integration contract. Focused release-automation tests passed (18/18); the complete quality:static chain passed, including exact 100% docstring enforcement, SDK boundary/parity, token budgets, context calibration, public surface, SDK entrypoint costs, and CLI transport floor."
  "2026-08-01T06:21:22.960Z","harness:codex","CI follow-up evidence (PR #850): decoded coverage shard 3 and found the second release-readiness package-script contract also retained the old 129 suppression budget. Aligned it to the burned-down 127 baseline. The focused packaging/prepublish contract and strict repo-wide ESLint pass."
  "2026-08-01T06:45:23.199Z","harness:codex","Review-fix evidence for PR #850: hardened the SDK-to-CLI boundary against package self-references, TypeScript import-type nodes, and computed import/require expressions inside SDK ownership files; added numeric tokenBudget/priority and snake-case create alias preservation; made the calibration gate compare its measured report to the reviewed checked-in baseline; removed dead mocks; and made CLI/MCP provenance parity require actual history entries. Focused regression validation passes 116/116. The PM review corrections also link and execute the calibration specification, replace a stale pre-fix file note, and preserve intentional multi-kind graph edges."
  "2026-08-01T06:57:04.666Z","harness:codex","Exact review-fix verification: the complete sandboxed suite passes 411 files and 6,652 tests at exact 46,836/33,707/9,540/45,468 statement/branch/function/line coverage (100/100/100/100). Strict lint passes ESLint, zero jscpd clones, static and 100% docstring quality, package boundary/parity, token and calibration gates, SDK surface/import-cost checks, and CLI transport floors."
  "2026-08-01T07:27:52.315Z","harness:codex","Exact-head CI diagnosis and remediation evidence: the initial Linux and Windows gates exposed platform-dependent byte/token measurements in the context-intent calibration report. Replaced byte-identical report comparison with a reviewed 15% regression ceiling while preserving exact contract shape, intent names, declared budgets, degradation order, cursor rows, and fail-closed declared token/byte bounds. A randomized cursor fuzz case also exposed an overly narrow test oracle; the implementation correctly distinguishes malformed cursors from syntactically valid but unsupported payloads, and the property now accepts both documented rejection classes. Verification: focused fuzz suite passed three independent runs; node scripts/run-tests.mjs coverage passed 411 files / 6653 tests at 100% statements (46872/46872), branches (33718/33718), functions (9544/9544), and lines (45503/45503); pnpm lint passed ESLint, zero duplicated lines/tokens, 100% docstring gates, SDK/package/token/calibration/gate-registry/surface/import-cost/transport gates; pnpm security:scan passed."
learnings[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-31T14:28:52.007Z","harness:claude-code","Counting import directions between two layers gives a precise answer to an architectural question that usually gets a qualitative one. Here 86 CLI-to-SDK imports against 36 SDK-to-CLI imports across 3 files reads as nearly-done until the 36 are enumerated and turn out to be the entire item lifecycle - so the useful metric is which capabilities flow the wrong way, not how many files do."
  "2026-08-01T05:27:11.941Z","harness:codex","Architecture boundary lesson: moving files is insufficient if logical SDK subpath barrels do not export the newly owned operations. Packed consumer assertions caught the gap; aggregate, query, and governance entrypoints must be validated independently from source imports and the root SDK barrel."
